{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nOn 2026-08-31 (~17:30-18:00 PDT), three consecutive MCP log_session writes failed with: `flock: could not acquire lock after 181s (holder: host=boot-bf4c34b1-475c-4363-8ff6-aada80c3c3ab pid=49003 start=19655570 held=155-174s pid_state=live op=compact-sweep)`.\n\nExecuted incident evidence:\n- `ps -p 49003` on the operator host found no process.\n- `lsof /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock` found no holder.\n- `held=` values were non-monotonic with constant `start`, consistent with a stale stamp.\n- Immediate local CLI `rebar session-log append` on the shared checkout succeeded, so this is specific to the MCP write path / MCP tracker clone.\n\n## Confirmed root cause\n\nMCP `log_session` uses the shared write-lock path: MCP tool -> `rebar.append_session_log` -> `session_log.append` -> `append_event` -> `lock.write_lock`. `lock.acquire` first obtains the kernel `.ticket-write.lock` fcntl leg, then polls the mkdir stamp dir `.ticket-write.lock.d`; on timeout it renders `.ticket-write.lock.d/owner` through `describe_lock_holder`.\n\nThe stale mkdir owner stamp is treated as authoritative for the whole write timeout even after the waiter has acquired the kernel fcntl leg. For same-host/same-namespace v2 stamps, `_stamp_is_stale` probes the pid. If `_pid_alive(pid)` is true but `_process_start_time(pid)` is unavailable, it waits for the 1h stale ceiling. That fixed the unbounded wedge in `larval-tribal-tigermoth`, but the 1h ceiling exceeds MCP/write request budgets, so every MCP write can still burn its full timeout while the kernel lock is free.\n\nDiagnostics have a matching gap: `_describe_stamped_pid` reports bare `_pid_alive(pid)` as `pid_state=live` without start-time corroboration, so a recycled/unqualified pid number is presented as a live holder even though it does not prove the stamped compact-sweep owner exists.\n\n## Runtime proof\n\nIn `/Users/joeoakhart/storelock-fix`, an isolated scratch repo forged `.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock.d/owner` as a same-host `op=compact-sweep` v2 stamp. The experiment first acquired `.ticket-write.lock` with nonblocking `fcntl`, proving the kernel lock was free, then drove real in-process FastMCP `log_session`. Instrumentation showed `_acquire_fcntl` succeeded, `_pid_alive(49003)` returned true, `_process_start_time(49003)` returned `None`, and the tool timed out with `pid_state=live`. A real MCP `rebar-log_session` call in this session timed out, while local CLI append immediately created `oxymoronic-ammonic-bats`; the shared checkout had no `.ticket-write.lock.d`, so the deployed MCP server is using a different tracker path/clone than the local CLI.\n\n## Defect attribution\n\n`caused_by`: `larval-tribal-tigermoth` (`ab00-1407-2da3-42fd`) by plan-defect/omission. That fix explicitly considered immediate reclaim when the fcntl leg is held and deliberately left it out; this incident proves the deferred case is necessary for MCP/write budgets. Close with `--class=plan_defect --caused-by=larval-tribal-tigermoth`.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nEdit only `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py` plus regression tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] MCP `log_session` with a forged same-host compact-sweep mkdir owner stamp completes promptly after acquiring the free kernel fcntl leg.\n- [ ] The regression test proves the free kernel fcntl leg was acquired before stale mkdir reclaim.\n- [ ] A same-host v2 stamp whose pid probe is unqualified (`_pid_alive` true, `_process_start_time` unavailable) is stale immediately when `fcntl_held=True`.\n- [ ] The same unqualified stamp remains refused while fresh when `fcntl_held=False`.\n- [ ] Holder diagnostics do not render an unqualified pid-number match as `pid_state=live`.\n- [ ] Holder diagnostics render a corroborated matching start time as `pid_state=live`.\n- [ ] Holder diagnostics render a differing known start time as a recycled/not-owner pid.\n- [ ] Existing lock tests still pass for corroborated-live owners, foreign-host stamps, malformed stamps, and aged unprovable stamps.\n- [ ] Step-7 parity census enumerates CLI, MCP/API, library facade, automated callers, dual-direction diagnostics, reconciler ref lock, and heartbeat/stamped-file locks.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py -q`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py -q`\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788238503203806001,"uuid":"4c16555d-85a4-4f14-8131-03cf8a2a27d2"}